I cannot find them in source file anywhere :disappointed:

@domenic, I just want to clarify one more question here.
Right now I put most of the styles within `@media (max-width: 30em)` that is equal to `480px` which does not fit most of the phones landscape mode (iPhone6 - `667 x 375`, Nexus 5 - `640 x 360`). So we probably should get bigger `@media` breakpoint, as an example bootstrap uses `767px = 47.9375em`.
Please let me know what you think about this.

@domenic 

> I kind of think it's better as-is, actually. Most people don't collapse the boxes. When you resize your browser window to be smaller (e.g. half-screen), you probably start getting annoyed by the boxes and having to collapse them one by one. Having them all flip at once and then become opt-in on smaller screens makes a lot of sense to me.

Right, I was suggesting a tri-state: by default if the user doesn't click anywhere, the behavior is the same as now (collapsed on small viewports, open on big viewports). It's just if the user clicks, the state would be maintained. Consider if the user starts with a big viewport, gets annoyed by a caniuse box and collapses it, then shrinks the window. With the current setup the annoying caniuse box would flip to being open in the narrow viewport layout.
